 and Doubt","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Questions and Doubt","type":"ThemeNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.1-43.5","r":"Ps.42.1-43.5","rawR":"Ps.42.1-43.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.1-43.5","value":"Ps.42.1-43.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 42–43"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," These psalms, like ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.9.1-20","r":"Ps.9.1-20","rawR":"Ps.9.1-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.9.1-20","value":"Ps.9.1-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 9"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.10.1-18","r":"Ps.10.1-18","rawR":"Ps.10.1-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.10.1-18","value":"Ps.10.1-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"10"},", form a unit comprising a lament with a bittersweet refrain of hope (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.5","r":"Ps.42.5","rawR":"Ps.42.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.5","value":"Ps.42.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:5"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.11","r":"Ps.42.11","rawR":"Ps.42.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.11","value":"Ps.42.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.43.5","r":"Ps.43.5","rawR":"Ps.43.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.43.5","value":"Ps.43.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"43:5"},"). In many Hebrew manuscripts these two psalms are combined as one. The historical context is uncertain; these psalms might be the voice of God’s people in exile, confessing their loyalty to God as he punishes them for their prevailing apostasy. The psalmist longs for fellowship with God such as he enjoyed in Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.4","r":"Ps.42.4","rawR":"Ps.42.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.4","value":"Ps.42.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:4"},"); his memories only make him more discouraged. As the psalmist cries out to God, he recalls God’s love and faithfulness (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.8","r":"Ps.42.8","rawR":"Ps.42.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.8","value":"Ps.42.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:8"},"), which moves him to plead for vindication (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.43.1-4","r":"Ps.43.1-4","rawR":"Ps.43.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.43.1-4","value":"Ps.43.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"43:1-4"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.42.1-43.5","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":43,"endVerse":5,"startChapter":42,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.42.1-43.5","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[42,43],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2cc37f14c4c4fe9a768dd53b0f3dc76e8585d7ee7a255fdef0e62a9f86cb640a","sourceItemName":"Ps.42.1-43.5","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6425,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.42.1-43.5","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.42.1-43.5","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.43.1-4","r":"Ps.43.1-4","rawR":"Ps.43.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.43.1-4","value":"Ps.43.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"43:1-4"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist turns to the Lord for rescue from his troubles, for guidance, for restoration, and for vindication."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.43.1-4","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":43,"endVerse":4,"startChapter":43,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.43.1-4","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[43],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"31610b4c70c375f0829aec3299e894f2b74f2ee3366bcf0421f484c6a8298e48","sourceItemName":"Ps.43.1-4","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6436,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.43.1-4","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.43.1-4","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.43.2","r":"Ps.43.2","rawR":"Ps.43.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.43.2","value":"Ps.43.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"43:2"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["tossed me aside:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," Other psalms similarly ask whether God has rejected his people (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.44.9","r":"Ps.44.9","rawR":"Ps.44.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.44.9","value":"Ps.44.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"44:9"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.44.23","r":"Ps.44.23","rawR":"Ps.44.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.44.23","value":"Ps.44.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.60.1","r":"Ps.60.1","rawR":"Ps.60.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.60.1","value":"Ps.60.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"60:1"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.60.10","r":"Ps.60.10","rawR":"Ps.60.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.60.10","value":"Ps.60.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.74.1","r":"Ps.74.1","rawR":"Ps.74.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.74.1","value":"Ps.74.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"74:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.77.7","r":"Ps.77.7","rawR":"Ps.77.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.77.7","value":"Ps.77.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"77:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.88.14","r":"Ps.88.14","rawR":"Ps.88.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.88.14","value":"Ps.88.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"88:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.89.38","r":"Ps.89.38","rawR":"Ps.89.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.89.38","value":"Ps.89.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"89:38"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.108.11","r":"Ps.108.11","rawR":"Ps.108.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.108.11","value":"Ps.108.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"108:11"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.43.2","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":43,"endVerse":2,"startChapter":43,"startVerse":2}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.43.2","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[43],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"c15fd5e7ce70d4e1670d3b3b0212e9d55dad8bc092763949156ac2601d4ec56c","sourceItemName":"Ps.43.2","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6437,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.43.2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.43.2","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.43.3","r":"Ps.43.3","rawR":"Ps.43.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.43.3","value":"Ps.43.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"43:3"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," In this prayer for God’s redemption, ",{"c":["light"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," and ",{"c":["truth"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," are viewed as guides (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.18.25-29","r":"Ps.18.25-29","rawR":"Ps.18.25-29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.18.25-29","value":"Ps.18.25-29"}],"t":"ref","v":"18:25-29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.27.1","r":"Ps.27.1","rawR":"Ps.27.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.27.1","value":"Ps.27.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"27:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.85.10-13","r":"Ps.85.10-13","rawR":"Ps.85.10-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.85.10-13","value":"Ps.85.10-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"85:10-13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.89.14-18","r":"Ps.89.14-18","rawR":"Ps.89.14-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.89.14-18","value":"Ps.89.14-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"89:14-18"},"; see also ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.119.105","r":"Ps.119.105","rawR":"Ps.119.105","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.119.105","value":"Ps.119.105"}],"t":"ref","v":"119:105"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.3.19","r":"John.3.19","rawR":"John.3.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.3.19","value":"John.3.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"John 3:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Eph.5.8","r":"Eph.5.8","rawR":"Eph.5.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eph.5.8","value":"Eph.5.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eph 5:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Thes.5.5-7","r":"1Thes.5.5-7","rawR":"1Thes.5.5-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Thes.5.5-7","value":"1Thes.5.5-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Thes 5:5-7"},"). • The Temple on the ",{"c":["mountain"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," in Jerusalem symbolized God’s ",{"c":["holy"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," presence among his people (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.15.1","r":"Ps.15.1","rawR":"Ps.15.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.15.1","value":"Ps.15.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 15:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.43.3","r":"Ps.43.3","rawR":"Ps.43.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.43.3","value":"Ps.43.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"43:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.99.5","r":"Ps.99.5","rawR":"Ps.99.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.99.5","value":"Ps.99.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"99:5"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.99.9","r":"Ps.99.9","rawR":"Ps.99.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.99.9","value":"Ps.99.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.132.7","r":"Ps.132.7","rawR":"Ps.132.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.132.7","value":"Ps.132.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"132:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.43.3","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":43,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":43,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.43.3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[43],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"966f5780382afc29985267e1246086902bd260f84a5759948529d9a9587b84d9","sourceItemName":"Ps.43.3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6438,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.43.3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.43.3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_ref